40965168,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"Twenty-four clinical isolates with non-B or B HIV-1 subtype were assessed for their in vitro susceptibility to LEN and their potential to develop resistance to LEN in viral breakthrough experiments. Clinical samples with diverse HIV-1 subtypes were used to evaluate the susceptibility to LEN across these subtypes, and resistance selection with LEN in samples with various HIV-1 subtypes were conducted.",The paper mentions that clinical isolates with non-B or B HIV-1 subtype were assessed for their in vitro susceptibility to LEN and their potential to develop resistance to LEN in viral breakthrough experiments. This indicates that HIV sequences from patient samples were used in the study.
40965168,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"Drug susceptibilities of the 24 clinical isolates were characterized in the MT-2 multicycle phenotypic assay. The overall mean LEN   EC50  for all viral isolates was 0.067  nmol / 1  (standard deviation [SD]: 0.027). The mean  EC50  of control drugs DTG, DRV, TAF, and EFV (representative drugs from the four main classes of antiretroviral drugs: integrase strand-transfer inhibitor, protease inhibitor, nucleotide reverse transcriptase inhibitor, nonnucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor [NNRTI], respectively), were 3.2  nmol / 1  (SD: 2.0), 6.0  nmol / 1  (SD: 3.8), 8.3  nmol / 1  (SD: 4.8) and 3.7  nmol / 1  (SD: 2.3), respectively, all within the expected range of  EC50  measurements.",The paper includes data on the in vitro drug susceptibility of HIV-1 isolates to lenacapavir (LEN) and control drugs using a multicycle phenotypic assay.
40965168,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide GenBank accession numbers.,The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.,The paper focuses on the in vitro studies and resistance selection of lenacapavir but does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
40965168,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The gene sequenced includes gag and protease gene, also CA and RT sequenced in viral breakthrough specimens.","The HIV-1 gag-protease DNA fragment from various HIV-1 isolates was cloned (pXXLAI vector), and viruses were generated by transfection. The capsid and reverse transcriptase sequence from the selected viruses were analyzed to determine the presence of resistance mutations.",The paper mentions the sequencing of the gag-protease fragment and the capsid and reverse transcriptase regions to determine resistance mutations.
40965168,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The specific countries are not mentioned in the paper, but the samples were from multiple clinical trials.","Patient plasma samples were obtained from studies GS-US-380-1490, GS-US-292-0104, GS-US-200-4334, and GS-US-200-4625.","The paper lists the clinical trials from which the samples were obtained, but does not specify the countries."
40965168,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The specific years are not mentioned in the paper.,The paper does not provide specific years for when the samples were obtained.,The paper focuses on the in vitro studies and resistance selection of lenacapavir but does not provide specific years for the sample collection.
40965168,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The method was Sanger sequencing.,"The plasmid DNA was prepared (Qiagen, #27104), followed by restriction enzyme digest with SfoI and XmaI and ligation with T4 DNA ligase (New England Biolabs, #M0467S) into wildtype pXXLAI linearized with the same enzymes. The ligated vector was used to transform stable competent cells (New England Biolabs, #C3040H). The transformed bacteria were grown overnight, and the plasmid DNA was purified and sequenced at ELIM Biopharmaceuticals (Hayward, California, USA).","The paper mentions that the plasmid DNA was purified and sequenced at ELIM Biopharmaceuticals, which indicates Sanger sequencing was performed."
40965168,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,Yes,"The HIV-1 gag-protease fragment from these plasma samples was amplified by two rounds of 30 cycles of PCR and subcloned into Zero Blunt TOPO pCR vector (Thermo Fisher, #450031). The obtained vector was used to transform one shot TOP10 chemically competent cells (Thermo Fisher, #C404003), and colonies of interest were grown overnight. The plasmid DNA was prepared (Qiagen, #27104), followed by restriction enzyme digest with SfoI and XmaI and ligation with T4 DNA ligase (New England Biolabs, #M0467S) into wildtype pXXLAI linearized with the same enzymes. The ligated vector was used to transform stable competent cells (New England Biolabs, #C3040H). The transformed bacteria were grown overnight, and the plasmid DNA was purified and sequenced at ELIM Biopharmaceuticals (Hayward, California, USA).",The paper describes the process of subcloning the amplified gag-protease fragment into a plasmid vector prior to sequencing.
40965168,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples were sequenced.,"Patient plasma samples were obtained from studies GS-US-380-1490, GS-US-292-0104, GS-US-200-4334, and GS-US-200-4625.",The paper specifies that patient plasma samples were used for sequencing.
40965168,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"Clinical samples were from participants who were treatment naive to the capsid inhibitor class, had diverse HIV-1 subtypes (A, A1, AE, AG, B, C, D, F1, G, H), and had HIV-1 RNA ranging from 3130 to 647000 copies/ml.","The paper mentions that the samples were from treatment-naive participants, which means they had not experienced virological failure on a treatment regimen."
40965168,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes,"Patient plasma samples were obtained from studies GS-US-380-1490, GS-US-292-0104, GS-US-200-4334, and GS-US-200-4625.",The paper lists the clinical trials from which the samples were obtained.
40965168,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,24,Twenty-four clinical isolates with non-B or B HIV-1 subtype were assessed for their in vitro susceptibility to LEN and their potential to develop resistance to LEN in viral breakthrough experiments. The gag-protease DNA fragment from a total of 24 patient samples was cloned into pXXLAI,"The paper mentions that 24 clinical isolates were used for the assessment, which means samples from 24 individuals were obtained."
40965168,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"Clinical samples were from participants who were treatment naive to the capsid inhibitor class, had diverse HIV-1 subtypes (A, A1, AE, AG, B, C, D, F1, G, H), and had HIV-1 RNA ranging from 3130 to 647000 copies/ml.","The paper specifies that the participants were treatment-naive to the capsid inhibitor class, which means they had not previously received ARV drugs."
40965168,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"Clinical samples were from participants who were treatment naive to the capsid inhibitor class, had diverse HIV-1 subtypes (A, A1, AE, AG, B, C, D, F1, G, H), and had HIV-1 RNA ranging from 3130 to 647000 copies/ml.","The paper specifies that the participants were treatment-naive to the capsid inhibitor class, which means they had not previously received any ARV drugs."
