41023944,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"We included HIV-positive individuals on dolutegravir (DTG)-based antiretroviral therapy (ART) who experienced virological failure, defined as HIV RNA > 1000 copies/mL, between June 1, 2023, and December 31, 2024. According to DREAM protocols, individuals with virological failure were enrolled in a six-month enhanced adherence support program; no ART regimen changes are made during the enhanced adherence support phase. A repeated viral load test was performed after this period, and those with persistent viremia (>1000 copies/mL) were eligible for genotypic resistance testing. Only individuals on DTG-containing regimens at the time of resistance testing were included in this analysis.","The study mentioned the collection of samples from HIV-positive individuals on DTG-based ART who experienced virological failure, indicating the presence of HIV sequences from patient samples is reported in the paper. The genotypic resistance testing involved sequencing of the HIV integrase region and other regions when available, confirming that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
41023944,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"In the considered period, 28 individuals on DTG-based ART who underwent resistance testing following confirmed virological failure (HIV RNA ∈ 1000 copies/mL) after six months of enhanced adherence support were included in the analysis. These represent all individuals for whom genotypic resistance test results were available, although additional eligible individuals did not receive testing due to logistical constraints. Among them, 13 (46.4%) had evidence of resistance to DTG, while 15 (53.6%) remained susceptible.",The paper focuses on genotypic resistance testing and the prevalence of resistance mutations among individuals failing DTG-based therapy. It mentions resistance mutations identified through sequencing but does not provide in vitro drug susceptibility data.
41023944,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No,The study does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates. It focuses on the resistance testing results and the prevalence of mutations without providing specific accession numbers.,"The content of the paper does not include any mention of GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, nor does it provide any information about submitting sequences to GenBank."
41023944,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"Integrase gene,Proviral DNA.","Resistance mutations were identified in the integrase region, and, when available, in the reverse transcriptase and protease regions. Resistance testing followed standardized DREAM protocols. Plasma samples from participants with confirmed virological failure were collected and sent to the Zimpeto DREAM laboratory, where viral RNA was extracted and amplified using an in-house reverse transcription and nested PCR method. Sequencing of the HIV integrase region was performed using the Sanger method at INQABA Biotechnical Industries, South Africa.","The paper mentions sequencing of the HIV integrase region and, when available, in the reverse transcriptase and protease regions, indicating that these genes were sequenced in the study."
41023944,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Mozambique,"This is a retrospective observational study conducted across five centers of the DREAM program in Mozambique, including two centers in Maputo City, one in Maputo Province, and two in Sofala Province. The DREAM program is a community-based, primary care HIV initiative that integrates clinical follow-up, laboratory monitoring, and social support, and has been active in Mozambique since 2002. Resistance testing followed standardized DREAM protocols. Plasma samples from participants with confirmed virological failure were collected and sent to the Zimpeto DREAM laboratory, where viral RNA was extracted and amplified using an in-house reverse transcription and nested PCR method. Sequencing of the HIV integrase region was performed using the Sanger method at INQABA Biotechnical Industries, South Africa.","The study was conducted in Mozambique, and the samples were obtained from the DREAM program centers in the country."
41023944,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2023-2024,"We included HIV-positive individuals on dolutegravir (DTG)-based antiretroviral therapy (ART) who experienced virological failure, defined as HIV RNA > 1000 copies/mL, between June 1, 2023, and December 31, 2024. Resistance testing followed standardized DREAM protocols. Plasma samples from participants with confirmed virological failure were collected and sent to the Zimpeto DREAM laboratory, where viral RNA was extracted and amplified using an in-house reverse transcription and nested PCR method. Sequencing of the HIV integrase region was performed using the Sanger method at INQABA Biotechnical Industries, South Africa.","The study included individuals who experienced virological failure between June 2023 and December 2024, indicating that the samples were obtained during these years."
41023944,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"Sequencing of the HIV integrase region was performed using the Sanger method at INQABA Biotechnical Industries, South Africa. Plasma samples from participants with confirmed virological failure were collected and sent to the Zimpeto DREAM laboratory, where viral RNA was extracted and amplified using an in-house reverse transcription and nested PCR method",The study specifies the use of the Sanger method for sequencing the HIV integrase region.
41023944,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,The study does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It focuses on the genotypic resistance testing and the sequencing results without providing details about any cloning procedures.,"The paper does not provide any information about cloning samples prior to sequencing, nor does it mention any cloning procedures."
41023944,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples,"Plasma samples from participants with confirmed virological failure were collected and sent to the Zimpeto DREAM laboratory, where viral RNA was extracted and amplified using an in-house reverse transcription and nested PCR method. Sequencing of the HIV integrase region was performed using the Sanger method at INQABA Biotechnical Industries, South Africa. Resistance testing followed standardized DREAM protocols.",The study mentioned the collection and sequencing of plasma samples from participants with confirmed virological failure.
41023944,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"We included HIV-positive individuals on dolutegravir (DTG)-based antiretroviral therapy (ART) who experienced virological failure, defined as HIV RNA > 1000 copies/mL, between June 1, 2023, and December 31, 2024. Resistance testing followed standardized DREAM protocols. Plasma samples from participants with confirmed virological failure were collected and sent to the Zimpeto DREAM laboratory, where viral RNA was extracted and amplified using an in-house reverse transcription and nested PCR method. Sequencing of the HIV integrase region was performed using the Sanger method at INQABA Biotechnical Industries, South Africa.","The study included individuals with confirmed virological failure on DTG-based ART, and sequences were obtained from these individuals."
41023944,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"This is a retrospective observational study conducted across five centers of the DREAM program in Mozambique, including two centers in Maputo City, one in Maputo Province, and two in Sofala Province. The DREAM program is a community-based, primary care HIV initiative that integrates clinical follow-up, laboratory monitoring, and social support, and has been active in Mozambique since 2002. The current analysis builds on a previously published cohort, expanding the sample by including all eligible participants who underwent genotypic resistance testing due to confirmed virological failure, even after an adherence reinforce intervention, while on DTG-based ART between July 2022 and December 2024.","The study is a retrospective observational study conducted in real-world settings, not a clinical trial."
41023944,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,28,"In the considered period, 28 individuals on DTG-based ART who underwent resistance testing following confirmed virological failure (HIV RNA ≥ 1000 copies/mL) after six months of enhanced adherence support were included in the analysis. These represent all individuals for whom genotypic resistance test results were available, although additional eligible individuals did not receive testing due to logistical constraints.",The study included 28 individuals who underwent resistance testing between June 2023 and December 2024.
41023944,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"We included HIV-positive individuals on dolutegravir (DTG)-based antiretroviral therapy (ART) who experienced virological failure, Resistance mutations were identified via Sanger sequencing and interpreted using the Stanford HIV Drug Resistance Database. Among all the 28 participants, 3 received rifampicin-based anti-tuberculosis treatment during DTG treatment, all of them modified DTG dosage according to guidelines; one of them developed DTG resistance.","The study included individuals on DTG-based ART who had experienced virological failure, indicating that they had previously received other ARV drugs."
41023944,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTIs, NNRTIs, PIs, INSTIs","We included HIV-positive individuals on dolutegravir (DTG)-based antiretroviral therapy (ART) who experienced virological failure, Resistance mutations were identified via Sanger sequencing and interpreted using the Stanford HIV Drug Resistance Database. Among all the 28 participants, 3 received rifampicin-based anti-tuberculosis treatment during DTG treatment, all of them modified DTG dosage according to guidelines; one of them developed DTG resistance. This study describes patterns of resistance to dolutegravir (DTG) and other drugs in treated individuals who experienced virological failure after at least six months of enhanced adherence support; resistance mutations were present in the integrase region and, when available, in the reverse transcriptase and protease regions, suggesting prior NSP, NRTI, PI exposure. Resistance was present regardless of reason for initiation of DTG-based therapy, including switching from other ART regimens due to virological failure. Clinical and demographic characteristics stratified by DTG susceptibility, including whether participants had experienced prior viral failure while on first generation NNRTIs, subsequent PI based regimens, or had started DTG based regimens due to viral suppression. All participants had virological failure while on DTG-based therapy, so were four NRTI naïve participants not included in the analysis.","The study included individuals failing a variety of regimens before DTG initiation, including NRTI, NNRTI, PI naïve. So the classes received before sequencing are NRTIs, NNRTIs and PIs."
41023944,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Rifampicin, Dolutegravir","We included HIV-positive individuals on dolutegravir (DTG)-based antiretroviral therapy (ART) who experienced virological failure, Resistance mutations were identified via Sanger sequencing and interpreted using the Stanford HIV Drug Resistance Database. Among all the 28 participants, 3 received rifampicin-based anti-tuberculosis treatment during DTG treatment, all of them modified DTG dosage according to guidelines; one of them developed DTG resistance. This study describes patterns of resistance to dolutegravir (DTG) and other drugs in treated individuals who experienced virological failure after at least six months of enhanced adherence support; resistance mutations were present in the integrase region and, when available, in the reverse transcriptase and protease regions, suggesting prior NSP, NRTI, PI exposure. Resistance was present regardless of reason for initiation of DTG-based therapy, including switching from other ART regimens due to virological failure. Clinical and demographic characteristics stratified by DTG susceptibility, including whether participants had experienced prior viral failure while on first generation NNRTIs, subsequent PI based regimens, or had started DTG based regimens due to viral suppression. All participants had virological failure while on DTG-based therapy, so were four NRTI naïve participants not included in the analysis.","The study mentions that 3 participants received rifampicin-based anti-tuberculosis treatment during DTG treatment, and all participants were on DTG-based ART, indicating these drugs were received before sample sequencing."
41023944,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,The study does not mention any deposition of sequences to public databases. It focuses on the resistance testing results and does not provide information on public availability of the sequences.,"The paper mentions that the datasets are available from the corresponding author on reasonable request, indicating that they are not publicly available."
41029850,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples. Individual samples with confirmed virological failure were sequenced in HIV-1 protease and reverse-transcriptase genes using Sanger sequencing and analysed using Stanford HIVdatabase.v.9.4.",Individual samples with confirmed virological failure were sequenced in HIV-1 protease and reverse-transcriptase genes using Sanger sequencing and analysed using Stanford HIVdatabase.v.9.4.,"The paper details the sequencing of HIV-1 protease and reverse-transcriptase genes from patient samples, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from these individuals."
41029850,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","GRT was performed in the pol gene (protease (PR) and reverse transcriptase (RT)) on the stored samples with plasma viral load ≥ 1000 copies/ml, using the previously validated inhouse protocol as described by Fokam et al. [21]. Sequences were assembled and edited using Recall v2.28 [22], interpreted using Stanford HIV drug resistance database (https://hivdb.stanford.edu/) version 8.5 and subtyping performed using rapid subtyping tools as previously described [23].",The paper focuses on genotypic resistance testing and does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility assays or results.
41029850,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,"The GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates include PQ893197, PQ893192, OQ985810, OR259747, and PQ893191.","However, sequences have been submitted to Genebank with available accession numbers provided (PQ893197, PQ893192, OQ985810, OR259747 and PQ893191) in the current version of the manuscript while the rest will be completed when made available by Genbank (submission ID: 2961867) (lines 451 to 455).",These accession numbers are explicitly listed in the supplementary information of the paper.
41029850,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The paper reports sequencing of the HIV-1 protease and reverse transcriptase genes in the pol gene region.,"GRT was performed in the pol gene (protease (PR) and reverse transcriptase (RT)) on the stored samples with plasma viral load ≥ 1000 copies/ml, using the previously validated inhouse protocol as described by Fokam et al. [21].","The genotypic resistance testing was performed in these two genes, as mentioned in the methods section."
41029850,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from Cameroon.,"This study describes patterns of acquired drug resistance (ADR) and potentially active drugs for subsequent ART regimens in individuals failing treatment in Cameroon. We conducted a cross-sectional, laboratory-based sentinel study among ART-failing individuals from October 2022 through April 2023 at the ""Chantal Biya"" International Reference Centre, Yaoundé-Cameroon.","The study was conducted in Cameroon, specifically at the 'Chantal Biya' International Reference Centre in Yaoundé."
41029850,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from 2022 to 2023.,"We conducted a cross-sectional, laboratory-based sentinel study among ART-failing individuals from October 2022 through April 2023 at the 'Chantal Biya' International Reference Centre, Yaoundé-Cameroon.",The study mentions the period during which the samples were collected.
41029850,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing was used for sequencing the HIV samples.,Individual samples with confirmed virological failure were sequenced in HIV-1 protease and reverse-transcriptase genes using Sanger sequencing.,The paper specifies the use of Sanger sequencing for the genotypic resistance testing.
41029850,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the paper does not mention that samples were cloned prior to sequencing.","Individual samples with confirmed virological failure were sequenced in HIV-1 protease and reverse-transcriptase genes using Sanger sequencing and analysed using Stanford HIVdatabase.v.9.4. Overall, 203 individuals were enrolled, median [IQR] age 37 [16-47] years with 58.1% (118/203) being female.","The cloning of samples prior to sequencing is not mentioned in the methods, indicating that this was not done."
41029850,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,The paper sequenced plasma viral load samples from individuals.,"GRT was performed in the pol gene (protease (PR) and reverse transcriptase (RT)) on the stored samples with plasma viral load ≥ 1000 copies/ml, using the previously validated inhouse protocol as described by Fokam et al. [21].","The samples were from plasma viral load, as indicated in the methods."
41029850,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.","A cross-sectional, laboratory-based sentinel study was conducted during the reporting period of March to April 2023 at the Chantal Biya International Reference Centre for research on HIV/AIDS prevention and management (CIRCB) in Yaoundé-Cameroon among ART-failing PWH. Participants were on documented ART for at least 12 months and experiencing virological failure (viral load ≥ 1000 copies/ml).","The study included ART-failing individuals with virological failure, and sequences were obtained from their samples."
41029850,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the paper does not mention that the patients were in a clinical trial.","A cross-sectional, laboratory-based sentinel study was conducted during the reporting period of March to April 2023 at the Chantal Biya International Reference Centre for research on HIV/AIDS prevention and management (CIRCB) in Yaoundé-Cameroon among ART-failing PWH. Participants were on documented ART for at least 12 months and experiencing virological failure (viral load ≥ 1000 copies/ml).","The study describes a cross-sectional sentinel surveillance, not a clinical trial."
41029850,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,203 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.,"Of 2109 individuals assessed, 203 met inclusion criteria, median age 37 [16-47] years and 118/203 (58.13%) females.",The paper states that 203 individuals met the inclusion criteria for the study.
41029850,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","A cross-sectional, laboratory-based sentinel study was conducted during the reporting period of March to April 2023 at the Chantal Biya International Reference Centre for research on HIV/AIDS prevention and management (CIRCB) in Yaoundé-Cameroon among ART-failing PWH. Participants were on documented ART for at least 12 months and experiencing virological failure (viral load ≥ 1000 copies/ml).","The study included individuals who were on documented ART for at least 12 months, indicating they had received ARV drugs."
41029850,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals received NRTIs, NNRTIs, and PIs before sample sequencing.","Overall, 203 individuals were enrolled, median [IQR] age 37 [16-47] years with 58.1% (118/203) being female. Median [IQR] duration on ART was 10 [6.9-13.3] years, with majority failing second-line (78.7%; 160/203). HIVDR rate was 85.3% (29/34) and 88.1% (140/160) in those failing first-line and second-line therapy respectively (p = 0.7).NNRTI, NRTI and PI/r resistance in individuals failing first-line ART was 85.3% (9/34), 82.4% (28/34) and 2.9% (1/34) respectively. In second-line failure, NNRTI, NRTI and PI/r resistance was 86.8% (138/160), 84.9% (135/160) and 47.17% (75/160) respectively.","Individuals were on various regimens, including NRTIs, NNRTIs, and PIs, indicating they received these drug classes before sample sequencing."
41029850,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals received drugs like ABC, 3TC, EFV, NVP, AZT, ATV/r, LPV/r, TDF, and DTG before sample sequencing.","Overall, median [IQR] duration on ART was 10 [6.9-13.3] years, with majority (160, 78.70%) on second-line, 34 (16.80%) on first-line and 9 (4.50%) on third-line. Detailed regimens included: ABC + 3TC + EFV/NVP (0.98%); AZT + 3TC + EFV/NVP (1.47) TDF + 3TC + EFV/NVP (6.89%); TDF + 3TC + DTG (7.39%%); AZT + 3TC + DTG (0.49%); ABC + 3TC + DTG (3.94%); ABC + 3TC + ATV/r (17.73%); ABC + 3TC + LPV/r (6.40%); AZT + 3TC + ATV/r (15.76%), AZT + 3TC + LVP/r (5.42%); TDF + 3TC + ATV/r (29.56%); TDF + 3TC + LPV/r (3.94%).","The paper lists various antiretroviral drugs received by individuals before sample sequencing, including NRTIs, NNRTIs, and PIs."
41029850,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"Yes, sequences from the paper were made publicly available.","However, sequences have been submitted to Genebank with available accession numbers provided (PQ893197, PQ893192, OQ985810, OR259747 and PQ893191) in the current version of the manuscript while the rest will be completed when made available by Genbank (submission ID: 2961867) (lines 451 to 455).","The paper mentions that the sequences have been submitted to GenBank, indicating their public availability."
41056006,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"HIV-1 capsid genotypic and phenotypic data were assessed at study entry using the GenoSure Gag-Pro and PhenoSense Gag-Pro assays (Monogram Biosciences). Resistance testing was performed for any participants who met one of the following virologic failure criteria: suboptimal virological response, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL and a decline of <1log10 from Day 1 to Week 10; virological rebound, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL after reaching <50 copies/mL, or two consecutive visits with an increase from nadir of >1log10; or participants with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL at last study visit.","The evidence clearly states that HIV-1 genotypic and phenotypic data were assessed, indicating that HIV sequences from patient samples were reported."
41056006,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"CLIBRATE study design assess final efficacy, safety, and emergent resistance with lenacapavir -resistant mutations emerged in four participants, no in vitro testing but consideirng assay and population, the drived sequence been in many other study, and mirrored, BbS regimen","The evidence indicates that resistance mutations were observed, but there is no mention of in vitro drug susceptibility testing being reported."
41056006,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No GenBank accession numbers were reported for the sequenced HIV isolates in the paper.,No genbank access number,"The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, as evidenced by the absence of such information in the methods or results sections."
41056006,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The HIV capsid gene was reported to have been sequenced.,HIV-1 capsid genotypic and phenotypic data were assessed at study entry using the GenoSure Gag-Pro and PhenoSense Gag-Pro assays (Monogram Biosciences).,The evidence indicates that the capsid region was sequenced for genotypic analysis.
41056006,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from the USA and the Dominican Republic.,"This study was approved by the institutional review board or ethics committee at all sites and was conducted in compliance with international laws and guidelines. Eligible participants were treatment naïve, ≥18 years old, and had screening plasma HIV-1 RNA of ≥200 copies/mL and CD4 cell counts of ≥200 cells/μL without active hepatitis B or C infection and Treatment-naive PwH were enrolled across 41 sites in the USA and Dominican Republic.",The evidence lists the USA and Dominican Republic as the locations where the samples were obtained.
41056006,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from between 2019 and 2020.,"Between 22 November 2019 and 27 August 2020, 183 participants in CALIBRATE were randomly assigned to one of four TGs.","The evidence provides a specific timeline for when the samples were collected, indicating the years 2019 to 2020."
41056006,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The paper does not specify the exact method of sequencing used for the HIV isolates.,No evidence,"The evidence indicates the genotypic and phenotypic were assessed by assay, without the specific sequencing method mentioned."
41056006,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,The paper does not mention whether samples were cloned prior to sequencing.,No evidence,There is no evidence in the paper that indicates the samples were cloned prior to sequencing.
41056006,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,The paper does not specify the type of clinical specimens that were sequenced.,No evidence,"The paper does not provide specific information on the type of clinical specimens that were sequenced, such as plasma or other biological materials."
41056006,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure.","Resistance testing was performed for any participants who met one of the following virologic failure criteria: suboptimal virological response, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL and a decline of <1log10 from Day 1 to Week 10; virological rebound, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL after reaching <50 copies/mL, or two consecutive visits with an increase from nadir of >1log10; or participants with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL at last study visit.–sixty-five virologic failure criteria met by 10 participants; Resistance mutations observed at Week 10, 28, 54, and/or 80 in six of these participants, or LEN RAM M184M/I in reverse transcriptase prior to Q67H + K70R in capsid at Week 10; Q67H at Week 54; and Q67H + K70R at Week 80 in 1 participant at each time point.",The evidence shows that resistance testing was done on individuals who met virologic failure criteria.
41056006,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"Yes, the patients were part of the CALIBRATE clinical trial.","CALIBRATE was a Phase 2, randomized, open-label, active-controlled, multicenter study.  This study was approved by the institutional review board or ethics committee at all sites and was conducted in compliance with international laws and guidelines.","The evidence confirms that the patients were part of a clinical trial, specifically the CALIBRATE study."
41056006,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,10 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.,"Of the 182 participants enrolled and dosed, 10 (6%) met virologic failure criteria and were included in the RAP","The evidence indicates that 10 participants met the resistance-associated mutation criteria, which implies samples were obtained for sequencing."
41056006,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, sequences were obtained from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","This study was approved by the institutional review board or ethics committee at all sites and was conducted in compliance with international laws and guidelines. Eligible participants were treatment naïve, and Resistance testing was performed for any participants who met one of the following virologic failure criteria: suboptimal virological response, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL and a decline of <1log10 from Day 1 to Week 10; virological rebound, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL after reaching <50 copies/mL, or two consecutive visits with an increase from nadir of >1log10; or participants with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL at last study visit, some  met the criteria and resistance testing.",The evidence indicates that resistance testing was done on individuals who met virologic failure criteria after receiving ARV drugs.
41056006,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals received integrase inhibitors (bictegravir, lenacapavir) and nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (emtricitabine, tenofovir alafenamide).","CALIBRATE was a Phase 2, randomized, open-label study (NCT04143594). Treatment-naive PWH were randomized (2:2:2:1) to four treatment groups (TGs): TG1 and TG2 received twice-yearly subcutaneous lenacapavir plus oral daily emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (F/TAF); TG3 received oral daily lenacapavir plus F/TAF; and TG4 received oral daily bictegravir/F/TAF; At W28, TG1 switched to lenacapavir plus TAF and TG2 switched to lenacapavir plus bictegravir. At W80, TG4 completed the study and TG1-3 continued assigned treatments.",The evidence outlines the specific ARV drugs and classes that were administered to the participants before sample sequencing.
41056006,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals received lenacapavir, emtricitabine, tenofovir alafenamide, and bictegravir.","CALIBRATE was a Phase 2, randomized, open-label study (NCT04143594). Treatment-naive PWH were randomized (2:2:2:1) to four treatment groups (TGs): TG1 and TG2 received twice-yearly subcutaneous lenacapavir plus oral daily emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (F/TAF); TG3 received oral daily lenacapavir plus F/TAF; and TG4 received oral daily bictegravir/F/TAF; At W28, TG1 switched to lenacapavir plus TAF and TG2 switched to lenacapavir plus bictegravir. At W80, TG4 completed the study and TG1-3 continued assigned treatments.","The evidence lists the exact drugs administered to the participants, confirming that these drugs were received before sequencing."
41056006,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"Data availability statement, Data requests should be sent to datarequest@gilead.com.","Data availability statement, Gilead Sciences shares anonymized individual participant data upon request or as required by law or regulation with qualified external researchers based on submitted curriculum vitae and reflecting non-conflict of interest. The request proposal must also include a statistician. Approval of such requests is at Gilead Science's discretion and is dependent on the nature of the request, the merit of the research proposed, the availability of the data, and the intended use of the data. Data requests should be sent to datarequest@gilead.com.","The evidence provides a contact for data requests, indicating that the sequences may be made available upon request."
41057785,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper mentions that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples.",Methods This cohort study retrospectively reviewed medical records of 235 People living with HIV (PLHIV) who underwent HIV drug resistance testing at the Mildmay-Uganda Hospital from 2018 to 2023.,"The study included a cohort of 235 PLHIV who underwent HIV drug resistance testing, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
41057785,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","Conclusion Drug resistance is common among PLHIV failing ART, dominated by NNRTI and NRTI mutations. DRMs were present among PLHIV who took a longer time to virological failure. Delayed failure was independently associated with older age, longer ART duration, and PI mutations. Findings support early DRM testing and individualized ART, especially as newer ART options emerge.",The paper focuses on clinical outcomes and drug resistance mutations without mentioning specific in vitro susceptibility testing results.
41057785,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.,No evidence,The paper does not mention GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
41057785,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The paper does not specify which HIV genes were sequenced, but it mentions drug resistance mutations in the context of different drug classes.","Prevalence of drug resistance mutations across ART regimen drug classes DRMs were detected in 140 of 235 participants (59.6%). NNRTI mutations were most prevalent at 52.8% (124/235; 95% CI: 46.4-59.2), followed by NRTI mutations at 50.2% (118/235; 95% CI: 43.8-56.6). PI major and accessory mutations were less frequent, 25.5% (60/235; 95% CI: 20.0-31.1) and 4.3% (10/235; 95% CI: 1.7-6.8), respectively. INSTI mutations were rare: 0.9% major (2/235; 95% CI: 0.3-2.0) and 0.4% accessory (1/235; 95% CI: 0.4-1.3)",The focus is on drug resistance mutations related to treatment regimens.
41057785,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The samples were obtained from Uganda.,"Methods This cohort study retrospectively reviewed medical records of 235 People living with HIV (PLHIV) who underwent HIV drug resistance testing at the Mildmay-Uganda Hospital from 2018 to 2023.   Study site and population This study was conducted at MUgH, a centre of excellence for HIV care and treatment in peri-urban Wakiso District, serving ∼15,000 PLHIV.","The study was conducted at Mildmay-Uganda Hospital, and the population characteristics reflect HIV care in Uganda."
41057785,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The samples were obtained from 2018 to 2023.,Methods This cohort study retrospectively reviewed medical records of 235 People living with HIV (PLHIV) who underwent HIV drug resistance testing at the Mildmay-Uganda Hospital from 2018 to 2023.,The study explicitly states that the samples were collected during this period.
41057785,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The paper does not specify the method used for sequencing.,No evidence,The paper does not provide details on the sequencing method employed.
41057785,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,The paper does not mention whether samples were cloned prior to sequencing.,No evidence,There is no mention of cloning samples in the sequencing process.
41057785,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,The paper does not specify the type of clinical samples sequenced.,No evidence,The paper does not provide details on the clinical type of specimens sequenced.
41057785,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure.","Methods This cohort study retrospectively reviewed medical records of 235 People living with HIV (PLHIV) who underwent HIV drug resistance testing at the Mildmay-Uganda Hospital from 2018 to 2023. In line with the HIV programmatic approach, PLHIV on ART who experienced virological failure were requested to undergo HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) testing.",The study focused on individuals who experienced virological failure and underwent drug resistance testing.
41057785,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the patients were not in a clinical trial.",Study design This cohort study retrospectively reviewed medical records of People living with HIV-1 who underwent HIV drug resistance testing at the Mildmay Uganda Hospital (MUgH) from 2018 to 2023.  Methods and materials  This cohort study retrospectively reviewed medical records of 235 People living with HIV (PLHIV) who underwent HIV drug resistance testing at the Mildmay-Uganda Hospital from 2018 to 2023.,"The study is a retrospective cohort study, not a clinical trial."
41057785,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,235 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.,Methods This cohort study retrospectively reviewed medical records of 235 People living with HIV (PLHIV) who underwent HIV drug resistance testing at the Mildmay-Uganda Hospital from 2018 to 2023.,The study explicitly states that 235 individuals were included.
41057785,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","In line with the HIV programmatic approach, PLHIV on ART who experienced virological failure were requested to undergo HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) testing. The study population comprised participants who had HIV drug resistance tests requested, with results uploaded to the Uganda HIVDR database.",The study included individuals who were on ART and underwent resistance testing.
41057785,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals received NRTI, NNRTI, PI, and INSTI drug classes.",Indication for DRM test PLHIV failing on first line 38(16.2%) PLHIV failing on second line 189(80.4%) PLHIV failing on third line 8(3.4%) Regimen at DRM testing NRTI + PI 78(40.6%) NRTI + INSTI(DTG) 65(33.9%) NRTI + INSTI(DTG&DVR/ETR) 6(3.1%) Others (ETR/DTG/DRV/R) 43(22.4%),The paper lists various drug regimens and classes used by the participants.
41057785,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,The paper does not specify the exact drugs received by individuals before sequencing.,No evidence,The paper does not provide a detailed list of specific drugs received by each individual.
41057785,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"Yes, the paper mentions that the data sets are available upon reasonable request.",Data availability The data sets for this study are available upon reasonable request from the corresponding author.,"The paper states that data sets are available upon request, indicating some level of public availability."
41088231,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples.","In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.","The evidence clearly states that the study identified HIV-1 sequences from patient samples, specifically from a plasma specimen of patient 230794."
41088231,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","Results The individual (230794) was 47 years old and got infected via heterosexual contact in Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province. The NFLG sequence of strain 230794 was 8260 nucleotides (nt) in length, with two CRF02_AG segments substituting in the backbone of subtype F2 in the vif and env gene regions. The genomic recombinant mosaic structures of 230794 were different from those of the other nine issued subtype F2/CRF02_AG URFs. No drug-resistant mutation was identified, but an INSTI other mutation, L74l, was identified. Strain 230794 was predicted to be a X4/R5 dual-tropism strain. Bayesian inference indicated that strain 230794 originated approximately between 2015 and 2018.",The paper focuses on the genetic characterization and recombination analysis of the HIV-1 strain and does not mention any in vitro testing of drug susceptibility.
41088231,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession number for the sequenced HIV isolate is PV187006.,"The NFLG sequence of 230794, which was 8260 nucleotides (nt) in length, was obtained and submitted to GenBank (accession number PV187006).",The evidence directly provides the GenBank accession number for the HIV sequence reported in the study.
41088231,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The near full-length genome (NFLG) of HIV-1 was sequenced.,The near full-length genome (NFLG) of HIV-1 was amplified with two overlapping segments by the near endpoint dilution method. The positive products were sequenced directly to obtain genomic sequences. The genomic recombinant mosaic structures of 230794 were different from those of the other nine issued subtype F2/CRF02_AG URFs. The V3-loop sequence of the NFLG was obtained using the GeneCutter tool.,"The paper mentions the sequencing of the near full-length genome, including the V3-loop region."
41088231,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from China.,"Specimen 230794 was collected in Oct. 2023 from a 47-year-old man who claimed to have contracted HIV-1 through heterosexual contact in Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province, China.","The evidence specifies the location of the sample collection, confirming that it was from China."
41088231,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained in 2023 and 2025.,"Specimen 230794 was collected in Oct. 2023 from a 47-year-old man who claimed to have contracted HIV-1 through heterosexual contact in Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province, China. According to national treatment strategies in China, the HIV patients on ART should be followed up to evaluate the ART efficacy. The patient 230794 obtained successful viral suppression with plasma viral load below the detection limit in 2025, therefore, we chose to harvest viral DNA from the whole blood sample.","The evidence provides information on the years when the samples were collected, indicating 2023 and 2025."
41088231,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing method was used.,"Positive products were directly purified and sequenced by Sangon Biotech (Shanghai) Co., Ltd with Sanger sequencing method.",The evidence explicitly mentions the Sanger sequencing method used in the study.
41088231,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, there is no indication that samples were cloned prior to sequencing.","Positive products were directly purified and sequenced by Sangon Biotech (Shanghai) Co., Ltd with Sanger sequencing method. The NFLG was assembled and cleaned by the software Sequencher","The process described does not include a cloning step, indicating direct sequencing of PCR products."
41088231,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma and whole-blood samples were sequenced.,"Viral RNA was extracted from the 2023 plasma sample using a magnetic bead-based method. Proviral DNA was extracted from the whole-blood sample collected in 2025 with the Viral DNA Extraction Kit (Supbio, China).",The evidence specifies the types of clinical specimens used for sequencing.
41088231,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"No, the paper does not mention sequences from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.","In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.",The paper focuses on treatment-naive individuals and their clinical sequencing data.
41088231,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the paper does not indicate that the patients were in a clinical trial.","In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.","The evidence shows that the patient was part of a surveillance study, not a clinical trial."
41088231,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,"One individual, patient 230794, had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.","In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.",The evidence indicates that only one patient sequence was reported and analyzed.
41088231,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"No, the paper does not report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.",The paper specifically mentions the drug naïve status of the individuals which indicated threre were no previously received ARV drugs.
41088231,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"No drug classes were received, individuals were antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive.","In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.","The evidence specifies that the individuals were ART-naive, meaning they had not received any ARV drugs."
41088231,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"No drugs were received before sample sequencing, individuals were antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive.","In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.","The evidence specifies that the individuals were ART-naive, meaning they had not received any ARV drugs."
41088231,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"Yes, the sequences were made publicly available in GenBank.","The NFLG sequence of 230794, which was 8260 nucleotides (nt) in length, was obtained and submitted to GenBank (accession number PV187006).",The evidence confirms that the sequence was submitted to a public database.
41091504,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"""The large number of drug-resistant sequences from patient samples and viral evolution experiments have resulted in a plethora of experimental data from us and others""",The paper discusses drug resistance mutations and their effects but does not present specific HIV sequences from patient samples.
41091504,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"""We have shown that the relationship between darunavir resistance and protease-inhibitor dynamics can be captured by linear regression models to predict loss of potency. For other systems, nonlinear methods may need to be implemented; however, we have shown that it is advantageous to try the most interpretable method first. The optimized strategy of MD-coupled machine learning provides a feasible method to consider all dynamic interactions of the enzyme-inhibitor complex, which is of particular importance for distal mutations in drug targets where clinical resistance can evolve. The strategy requires enzyme-inhibitor structure optimization, parallel MD simulations of the complexes, physical feature extraction, feature reduction with elastic net, and the generation of linear regression models, which are trained to predict experimental inhibitor potency from the MD-derived physical features (Figure 1).""","The paper focuses on molecular dynamics simulations and machine learning to predict drug resistance, without providing specific in vitro susceptibility results."
41091504,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not applicable,The study does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates.,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers as it does not report on sequenced isolates.
41091504,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Not applicable,The paper does not report on the sequencing of specific HIV genes.,"The focus is on molecular dynamics and machine learning, not on sequencing specific genes."
41091504,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Not applicable,The study does not mention any countries from which sequenced samples were obtained.,The paper does not provide information on the countries of origin for sequenced samples.
41091504,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,Not applicable,The study does not mention any years from which sequenced samples were obtained.,The paper does not provide a timeline for when samples were sequenced.
41091504,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Not applicable,The paper does not discuss any specific methods used for sequencing.,"The focus is on molecular dynamics and machine learning, not on sequencing methods."
41091504,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,Not applicable,The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.,The paper does not discuss any cloning of samples.
41091504,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Not applicable,The paper does not specify any type of clinical or laboratory samples.,The paper does not provide information on the type of clinical specimens sequenced.
41091504,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"In this study we are using a very potent inhibitor, darunavir, bound to a series of 28 variants of HIV-1 protease with affinities from picomolar to micromolar, to develop an accurate method for predicting resistance.",The paper does not mention any sequences from individuals with virological failure.
41091504,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,The study does not mention any clinical trials involving patients.,The paper does not provide information about whether patients were part of a clinical trial.
41091504,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,Not applicable,The study does not mention any individuals from whom samples were obtained for sequencing.,The paper does not provide information on the number of individuals involved.
41091504,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Not applicable,The study does not report on sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.,"The paper focuses on protease variants and their dynamics, not on individual patient histories."
41091504,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not applicable,The study does not mention any drug classes received by individuals.,The paper does not provide information on the drug classes received by individuals.
41091504,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not applicable,The study does not mention any specific drugs received by individuals.,The paper does not report on any specific drugs received by individuals.
